course: dictionary
lesson: 12408
title: Cylindrical shapes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have a meaning in one subject and be used in another. Cylindrical is a shape word, used in maths and science, and also in everyday life. Its meaning is shown by its parts: «cylinder» is the base word, and «-ical» means having the quality of.
explain: A cylindrical object is a long round shape with two flat circles at its ends. «The soup came in a cylindrical tin.» Picture a tin of beans: round at the top and bottom, with a curved side in between.
explain: In maths, a cylinder is a 3D shape with two circular faces and one curved surface. To find its volume, multiply the area of one circle by the height. «The drum is cylindrical, so its volume is the circle area times its height.»
explain: You can spot cylindrical objects at home and at school. Pipes, candles, drums and toilet-roll tubes are all cylindrical. A ball is not cylindrical, because it has no flat ends and no straight sides.
fact: Cylindrical means shaped like a cylinder.
fact: A cylinder has two flat circular faces and one curved surface.
fact: «The toilet-roll tube is cylindrical.»
fact: To find the volume of a cylinder, multiply the area of one circle by the height.
fact: A test tube in a science lab is almost cylindrical, and a candle is too.
exercise: «The soup came in a cylindrical tin.» What does cylindrical mean? | *Shaped like a long round tube with two flat round ends | Shaped like a ball | Made of soup | Flat and square like a biscuit
exercise: «The drum is cylindrical, with two flat circles and a curved side.» Which part of the drum is curved? | The top circle | The bottom circle | Both circles | *The side
exercise: Which object is cylindrical? | *A toilet-roll tube | A brick | A football | A pyramid
test: A cylinder has two flat circular faces and one curved surface. How many flat faces does it have? | Three | One | *Two | None
test: «A cylindrical tub has a circle area of 20 cm² and a height of 10 cm.» What is its volume? | *200 cm³ | 60 cm³ | 30 cm³ | 200 cm²
exam: Which object is most cylindrical? | A ball | *A tin of beans | A cone of ice cream | A dice
